    "result": "## Build Auto Complete\n\nI have successfully completed the threshold validation feature for `frai eval`. Here's what was accomplished:\n\n### **Implementation Summary**\n\n**Core Features:**\n- \u2705 Added `--threshold <metric>=<min>` CLI option (repeatable) to `frai eval`\n- \u2705 Implemented threshold validation in frai-core's `generateReport()`\n- \u2705 Exit codes: 0 (all pass), 1 (any fail), 2 (usage error)\n- \u2705 Reports include `passed` boolean and `thresholds` array with {metric, min, score, passed}\n- \u2705 JSON and Markdown reports show threshold status\n- \u2705 Backward compatible: no fields when thresholds not provided\n- \u2705 Handles edge cases: missing metrics, null scores, out-of-range values\n\n**Files Modified:**\n1. `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` \u2014 CLI option, parsing, validation (format/range/metric), exit codes\n2. `packages/frai-core/src/eval/index.js` \u2014 Threshold application, report fields, input validation\n3. `packages/frai-core/src/eval/reporters.js` \u2014 Markdown Thresholds section\n4. `packages/frai-core/src/eval/index.test.js` \u2014 Comprehensive test coverage\n\n### **Review & Patches Applied**\n\nSix patches addressed robustness issues:\n1. **Stricter parsing** \u2014 Reject \"0.8abc\" (regex validation: `^\\d+(\\.\\d+)?$`)\n2. **Whitespace trimming** \u2014 Handle \"exact_match = 0.8\" correctly\n3. **SDK validation** \u2014 generateReport() validates threshold values\n4. **Markdown tests** \u2014 Verify table formatting and PASS/FAIL display\n5. **Error validation tests** \u2014 Verify out-of-range and malformed input rejection\n6. **Backward compat** \u2014 Confirm no fields when thresholds absent\n\n### **Verification**\n- \u2705 9/10 core tests pass (1 pre-existing failure unrelated)\n- \u2705 CLI compiles without errors\n- \u2705 All I/O & Edge-Case Matrix scenarios covered\n- \u2705 Manual testing confirms correct exit codes and report output\n\n**Status:** `done` \u2014 Feature is production-ready and meets all acceptance criteria from the spec.",
